  "asr_text": "When I leave a notice saying nobody was home and head off, I feel a little down too. But then I go to the next house. I really would like to see fewer re-deliveries, and they are hard on us, too. Even so, I can't just say that customers should pay the cost. I think it makes more sense to cover the cost through the overall fee for carrying packages than to charge each customer who wasn't home for the cost of that re-delivery. To do that, I want the company to think about whether free shipping for online orders should stay as it is. If they review shipping fees, I want them to review how the fees are set, too, so that the money really reaches the people who deliver the packages.",
